      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9026100::rubric_card::000::8d31f456a8"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stationary friction processing enhances the oxidation resistance of AlCoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9026100::rubric_card::000::8d31f456a8"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The enhanced oxidation resistance is mediated by formation of protective oxide scales.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9026100::rubric_card::000::8d31f456a8"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher grain-boundary density facilitates rapid outward diffusion of Cr.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid outward diffusion of Cr promotes formation of a dense protective Cr2O3 layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An Al-rich oxide subsequently forms through inward oxygen diffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed protective oxide sequence limits formation of nonprotective spinel oxides.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation kinetics decrease by approximately 38–48% for samples processed at the higher rotational speed.",
